course: dictionary
lesson: 15054
title: Looking back on the past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Retrospection means thinking back about past events, or about your own past. It is the act of looking back. When you think about last summer and what you learnt from it, you are doing retrospection.
explain: Sometimes retrospection is used to judge something after it has happened. «In retrospect, I should have taken my coat.» The speaker is looking back now and seeing that a different choice would have been better.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. Words like «looking back», «remembering» and «after it happened» are a sign that the writer is using retrospection. Ask yourself: is the person thinking about the past?
fact: Retrospection means thinking back about past events.
fact: «In retrospect» means looking back now, after something has happened.
fact: «A moment of retrospection» is a short time spent thinking back about the past.
fact: Retrospection is an uncountable noun, so we say «some retrospection», not «a retrospection».
fact: Retrospection comes from the idea of looking back, so the word helps you remember that the past is behind you.
exercise: «Ella spent a quiet evening in retrospection, thinking about her first year at school.» What is Ella doing? | Planning a trip to the beach | Running to catch a bus | *Looking back on the past | Cooking her dinner
exercise: «In retrospect, the picnic was a bad idea, because the rain came early.» What does «in retrospect» mean here? | *Looking back now, after it happened | Before the picnic started | In a great hurry | Very quickly
exercise: Which word means looking back on the past? | Prediction | Ambition | *Retrospection | Invention
test: «In retrospect, Tom wished he had asked for help.» What does «in retrospect» tell you? | *Looking back, after it had happened | Before he did anything | Without thinking at all | At the very end of the race
test: Which of these is an example of retrospection? | Guessing what the weather will be like tomorrow | *Remembering last summer's holiday and what you learnt from it | Planning next summer's holiday | Counting the days until school ends
exam: «After the test, Maya had a moment of retrospection and saw she had rushed the last question.» Why did Maya think back? | To plan her next holiday | *To judge her test after it had happened | To invent a new game | To learn a new song
